# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# The repository is already LF throughout. Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true
# by default, which would check these files out as CRLF and silently rewrite them.
# That is harmless for the PowerShell files, but not for the ones that are mounted
# into the Linux containers: the *.sh scripts break outright, and docker/.env and
# docker/pgadmin-pgpass would carry a stray carriage return into a password.
#
# Pinning eol=lf here wins over core.autocrlf, so every clone gets the same files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images are never converted. Git detects this on its own, but being explicit
# means a future change to the line above cannot corrupt them.
*.jpg binary
